      "message": "1) validate token is returning 200 as created\u003dFalse by default. authenticate_for_token() set created\u003dTrue to return a 201\n2) Because we need to create a legitimate HTTP response. Content and its type will get translated correctly in the middleware, depending on the request. See https://github.com/openstack/keystone/blob/master/keystone/middleware/core.py#L144\n3) in v3, create token and validate token returns the exact same thing, different only in status (201 versus 200).",
